# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for scripts/sdk-sanitize.mjs.
#
# Every entry here is a finding somebody LOOKED AT and decided to leave, with
# the reason beside it. An entry without a reason is a finding being hidden.
#
# stb_vorbis (vendored, upstream v1.22): get32_packet assembles a value with
# `get8_packet(f) << 8`, and at end-of-packet get8_packet returns -1, so the
# shift is of a negative int -- undefined in C++17, and arithmetic on every
# compiler this SDK builds with. The value is discarded by the checks that
# follow. Upstream's code; not memory-unsafe; left alone so the vendored file
# stays upstream's byte for byte apart from the one fix marked in it.
shift-base:stb_vorbis.c
